(General Public Pollution Precautions & Action Guide) Tj T*

(Document ID: REF-PRE-2024) Tj T*
(Source: Center for Environmental Health & Protection) Tj T*
(Topic: Practical Precautions for Elevated AQI Levels) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Recommended Actions by AQI Tier:) Tj T*
(1. Moderate \(AQI 51-100\):) Tj T*
(   - Unusually sensitive individuals should consider limiting prolonged outdoor exertion.) Tj T*
(2. Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups \(AQI 101-150\):) Tj T*
(   - Children, elderly, and individuals with respiratory conditions should reduce outdoor activity.) Tj T*
(   - Wear N95 or KN95 respirators when near heavy traffic corridors.) Tj T*
(3. Unhealthy \(AQI 151-200\):) Tj T*
(   - Avoid prolonged or heavy exertion outdoors.) Tj T*
(   - Keep windows closed and run indoor air purifiers with HEPA filtration.) Tj T*
(   - Reschedule outdoor athletic events to early morning or indoor facilities.) Tj T*
(4. Very Unhealthy & Hazardous \(AQI > 200\):) Tj T*
(   - Remain indoors with high-efficiency particulate air filtration.) Tj T*
(   - Avoid all strenuous physical activity outdoors.) Tj T*
